med","webcast":false,"url":"https://blackburn.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-21","committee":"Children & Young People Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://blackburn.moderngov.co.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"Executive Board","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://blackburn.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-11","committee":"Executive Member Decisions","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://blackburn.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-14","committee":"Place Overview & Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://blackburn.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-18","committee":"Executive Member Decisions","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://blackburn.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-22","committee":"Audit & Governance Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://blackburn.moderngov.co.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Blackburn with Darwen's accounts unaudited for three years as council's finances improve","lead":"Blackburn with Darwen Council has been unable to obtain independent audit sign-off on its financial statements for three consecutive years, with audit opinions disclaimed in December 2024, February 2025 and February 2026 due to insufficient time to complete verification procedures. The council's auditors are now undertaking a \"rebuilding assurance\" process expected to span more than one audit cycle. Despite the absence of formal audit confirmation, the council's actual financial position has improved: net debt fell \u00a311.4m to \u00a387.5m in the first quarter of this year as the council increased cash holdings, and the cost of servicing debt fell from 7.3 per cent to 6.4 per cent of the council's revenue budget. The auditor has identified no significant weaknesses in the council's arrangements for financial sustainability, governance or efficiency, though the audit fee has risen 20 per cent to \u00a3309,655 to reflect the additional catch-up work required.","iso":"2026-09-22","paper_title":"Agenda Item 6 Blackburn with Darwen ASM 2526","paper_url":"https://blackburn.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s35429/35429.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Blackburn with Darwen's three-year audit gap ends but assurance over reserves still uncertain","lead":"The council has emerged from three consecutive years without audit sign-off on its financial statements, but material uncertainty now surrounds its reserve balances. The external auditor disclaimed opinions on 2022/23, 2023/24, and 2024/25 accounts because there was insufficient time to complete audit procedures. Because opening balances for 2025/26 remain unaudited, reserves\u2014money the council has set aside\u2014lack verification of what portion can actually be spent. The auditor is undertaking a \"rebuilding assurance\" process expected to span more than one audit cycle to restore normal audit sign-off. Audit fees have risen 20 per cent to \u00a3309,655, reflecting the additional catch-up work required. However, the auditor has identified no significant weaknesses in the council's arrangements for financial sustainability, governance, or efficiency in current-year planning procedures.","iso":"2026-09-22","paper_title":"Agenda Item 6 Blackburn with Darwen ASM 2526","paper_url":"https://blackburn.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s35429/35429.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Audit & Governance Committee","paper_title":"Agenda Item 10 - Risk Management 2026.2027 Q1 Update","paper_url":"https://blackburn.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s35432/35432.pdf","headline":"Medium Term Financial Strategy risk closed, indicating confidence in future financial position","detail":"Risk 16 regarding 'Failure to deliver a robust MTFS with adequate reserves' has been closed. This indicates the council now considers its Medium Term Financial Strategy adequate and its financial reserve position sound.","category":"reserves","matters":"MTFS confidence is a key financial health indicator; closure suggests the council has achieved sufficient financial planning and reserve adequacy","figures":"Risk 16 closed (previously tracked in corporate risk register)","quote":"Risk 16: Failure to deliver a robust Medium Term Financial Strategy (MTFS) with adequate reserves to meet unforeseen circumstances and with the resource capacity to deliver statutory services.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Audit & Governance Committee","paper_title":"Agenda Item 10 - Risk Management 2026.2027 Q1 Update","paper_url":"https://blackburn.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s35432/35432.pdf","headline":"New corporate risk for CCTV Code of Practice compliance and IT network infrastructure supporting CCTV","detail":"Risk 45, created May 2026, rated MEDIUM (Likelihood 3, Impact 3). Council has flagged both governance risk (Surveillance Camera Code of Practice compliance) and emerging operational concern regarding the stability of IT network infrastructure supporting CCTV systems across the council.","category":"governance","matters":"IT infrastructure risk affects operational capability and service continuity; CCTV governance failures create legal and reputational exposure","figures":"Risk 45: L3 I3 MEDIUM (new risk added in Q1)","quote":"The risk to the Council associated with any non-compliance with the Surveillance Camera Code of Practice and associated governance arrangements, and emerging concerns relating to the IT network infrastructure supporting the CCTV systems in place across the Council.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Audit & Governance Committee","paper_title":"Agenda Item 10 - Risk Management 2026.2027 Q1 Update","paper_url":"https://blackburn.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s35432/35432.pdf","headline":"Council's care services exposed to Lancashire & South Cumbria Integrated Care Board's budget deficit","detail":"Risk 33 remains HIGH (Likelihood 4, Impact 4) based on external dependency on the ICB's 2023/24 budget position and planned future savings. The ICB's deficit creates cascading risks for council-dependent care services and community wellbeing outcomes.","category":"demand","matters":"External dependency creates uncontrollable risk; if the ICB reduces services or funding, the council may face provision gaps or pressure to fund replacements","figures":"Risk 33: L4 I4 HIGH; ranks among the council's top three corporate risks","quote":"The potential negative impact on the delivery of the Council's care services and community wellbeing arising from the implications of Lancashire & South Cumbria's Integrated Care Board's 2023/24 budget deficit and associated savings plans for future years.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Audit & Governance Committee","paper_title":"Agenda Item 10 - Risk Management 2026.2027 Q1 Update","paper_url":"https://blackburn.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s35432/35432.pdf","headline":"Tree management liability rated HIGH with controls strength recorded as POOR\u2014only risk with lowest control rating","detail":"Risk 41, created August 2025, maintains HIGH rating (Likelihood 4, Impact 5) and is the only corporate risk with 'Poor' strength of existing controls. Represents potential liability for injury or property damage from tree failure on council-owned land. Council has engaged Zurich Resilience Solutions for support.","category":"governance","matters":"Poor control rating indicates a management gap in tree asset management; this operational and reputational risk could materialise as public claims or incident costs","figures":"Risk 41: L4 I5 HIGH; only corporate risk with 'Poor' control rating","quote":"Tree management: the uncontrolled failure of trees or their parts (branches, roots) located on council-owned or managed land leading to injury to members of the public or staff, or damage to property, which the Council is liable for and related damage to the Council's reputation.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Audit & Governance Committee","paper_title":"Agenda Item 10 - Risk Management 2026.2027 Q1 Update","paper_url":"https://blackburn.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s35432/35432.pdf","headline":"SEND High Needs Budget and EHCPs remain rated as second-highest corporate risk at HIGH","detail":"Risk 36 maintains HIGH residual rating (Likelihood 4, Impact 4) with no improvement from the previous quarter. This reflects ongoing budget pressures in special educational needs provision, a significant challenge requiring council support and reserve funding.","category":"overspend","matters":"SEND deficits typically require supplementary funding from general reserves; persistent HIGH rating indicates substantial budget strain in this statutory area","figures":"Risk 36: L4 I4 HIGH (unchanged from previous quarter)","quote":"SEND High Needs Budget and EHCPs","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-22"},"name":"Blackburn with Darwen UA","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-24","since_iso":"2026-08-25","distress":false,"headline":"Medium Term Financial Strategy risk closed, indicating confidence in future financial position","lead":"MTFS confidence is a key financial health indicator; closure suggests the council has achieved sufficient financial planning and reserve adequacy","also":["21 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Executive Member Decisions on 2026-09-25","n_findings":22,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Agenda Item 10 - Risk Management 2026.2027 Q1 Update","top_paper_url":"https://blackburn.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s35432/35432.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":91,"news_drafts_total":2}}